    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57559": {
      "title": "Parking Field Operations Manager",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Parking Field Operations Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Parking Field Operations Manager Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button.\r\n\r\nIf you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link.\r\nApplicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. \tThe information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested individuals should complete an online application and be prepared to upload the following documents at the time of application: 1. Current CV or Resume 2. Cover letter summarizing interest and qualifications for the role 3. List of 3 professional references including current telephone and email addresses for all references. For full consideration, please submit your materials by position closing date Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Business Title Parking Field Operations Manager Applications Accepted From University Wide, Public: Open to the Public Special Instructions to Applicants Interested individuals should complete an online application and be prepared to upload the following documents at the time of application: 1. Current CV or Resume 2. Cover letter summarizing interest and qualifications for the role 3. List of 3 professional references including current telephone and email addresses for all references. For full consideration, please submit your materials by position closing date This position is eligible for the following benefits: medical, vision, dental, basic and supplemental life, winter break closure, paid holidays, educational benefits for you and eligible dependents, sick leave, vacation, and retirement. Posting Number 2016479T Job Description Summary Department Summary The Parking Field Operations Manager oversees all campus parking enforcement and compliance operations, including parking citations, towing, booting, and vehicle relocation. The position also manages maintenance, inspection, and documentation of parking and road closure related field equipment and stats documentation to ensure safe, reliable, and efficient operations. The manager serves as a front-line ambassador for parking compliance and customer service while supporting field equipment needs for service programs and special events. Position Responsibilities: Oversee campus parking enforcement & compliance operations, including issuing and managing parking citations, towing, booting, and relocating vehicles in accordance with campus policies and safety regulations. Supervise up to 20 student enforcement officers and two FTE AFSCME 1699 field ambassadors responsible for citation issuance and enforcement activities. Schedule and oversee work assignments. Conducts employee/labor relations matters as necessary in alignment with university policy & contractual requirements and proactively works to diffuse potential conflict before it begins Serve as a visible, front-line ambassador promoting parking compliance, service awareness, and conflict resolution. Ensure compliance with state, federal, and local parking & ADA regulations. Monitor enforcement metrics and KPI’s to optimize patrol routes and resource allocation, measure field effectiveness, and identify areas for improvement focused on proactive rather than reactive parking management strategies. Manage maintenance, setup, and tear-down of field service equipment, including VMS boards, road closure devices, signage, electric vehicle charging stations, and digital pay stations. Conduct and document PCI inspections for all field equipment to ensure operational readiness, safety, and compliance with financial & regulatory standards. Coordinate equipment deployment and retrieval to support parking reservations, special events, and operational needs. Oversee preventive maintenance, repair schedules, and proper documentation of all field equipment. Oversee road closure processes in accordance with safety, Manual on Uniform Traffic Control Devices ( MUTCD ) and regulatory standards. Create and execute maintenance plans for parking lot striping and curb markings, supervise field work for lot painting and general maintenance activities Conduct in-field lot audits and facility utilization data collection efforts. Conduct and document pavement assessment condition indexing, parking signage and facility layouts & inspections for parking & equipment assets. Oversee integration of new enforcement technologies with existing parking management infrastructure. Remain current with emerging parking enforcement technologies and industry best practices to optimize service. Hire, train, and evaluate field ambassadors and student enforcement officers. Serves as the primary point of contact for after-hours support/resolution for assigned programs. Displays leadership that results in teamwork, customer focus, innovation and continuous process improvement within their organization. Serves as a liaison for Transportation & Parking Services operations, representing the unit in a professional and customer-centric manner. Assists with documentation of standard operating procedures, preventative maintenance schedules, departmental guidelines, professional development and training, and safety/emergency procedures for operations activities & personnel in compliance with university, bargaining unit, and state/federal regulations. Maintains operational inventories. Collaborates with senior leadership team and provides recommendations for leveraging data to optimize service offerings and programs. Assist with development of capital asset plans, and parking operational strategies. Supports special projects and initiatives for unit and RFP’s for parking technology as assigned. Provides coordination support for major event operations utilizing parking resources. Provides support and assist with departmental functions as needed. Performs other misc. duties as assigned. Works to resolve complex service issues & ensure operational efficiency and high levels of customer service with minimal impact to business operations and service functions. Position Profile Monitors campus transportation and parking activities and compliance with established policies. Responsible for overseeing permit parking, parking enforcement, event transportation, business transportation, campus transit service, safety and training, and facility and operations maintenance. Level Summary Supervises a team and ensures effective work activities within work unit. Has input on personnel actions for direct reports. Primarily focused on supervision, but may still engage in operational tasks similar to the direct reports’ roles. Accountable for the productivity and effectiveness of the team or department, ensuring goals are met. Supervisory Responsibilities Manages a small team. Directly oversees at least 2.0 FTE employees. Has authority to manage performance and assign duties. May have authority to hire, transfer, suspend, promote, discharge, reward, and discipline employees. Fiscal Responsibilities Responsible for managing a small budget or part of a larger budget. Problem Solving Solves interpersonal team issues and develops solutions for team-related problems. Seeks guidance from higher-level management on complex problems. Independence of Action Has discretion in decision-making but reports to higher-level management. Communication and Collaboration Collaborates with higher-level manager(s) and other teams, ensures team alignment with organizational goals. Physical Requirements Requires a range of physical activities. Positions may require driving, standing, walking through parking facilities, and/or ascending stairs or ramps. Minimum Qualifications Requires a Bachelor’s degree in a related field, 3 or more years of related professional experience, and 1 or more years of supervisory experience, or equivalent education and experience. Certain positions may require Commercial Driver’s License ( CDL ). Must possess a valid Driver’s License. Must possess or be able to obtain an underground storage tank ( UST ) class C Operator Certification with 30 days of employment (training provided). Preferred Qualifications Strong oral and written communications and must have proficient knowledge in Microsoft Office and technology. Ability to work under pressure managing multiple service priorities, strong interpersonal, organizational and teamwork skills. Experience with parking management technologies. Complex understanding of parking compliance and ADA parking requirements within 120 days of employment. Department Transportation & Parking Pay Rate The target salary range is $44,592 to $59,085 commensurate with the selected candidate’s education and experience while considering internal equity. Ohio University is proud to offer a robust healthcare plan that includes maternity care, counseling and mental healthcare, prescription coverage, vision, dental, orthodontia care, and more. Our robust benefits package also includes paid holidays, sick time, personal time, a tuition waiver up to 100% for self and dependents, an excellent retirement plan with up to a 14% employer contribution, a 12-week parental leave program, adoption reimbursement, flextime and flexplace policies, an employee assistance program, access to professional development programs, and additional employee resources. Additional information is available at https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits . Total Compensation Estimator (For Full-Time Benefits Eligible Employees) Discover the full value of joining Ohio University by clicking this link: https://www.ohio.edu/hr/compensation/total-compensation-estimator Our Total Compensation Estimator shows your offer package in dollars: salary plus university paid benefits including health coverage, retirement contributions, paid time off, tuition benefits, and more. See details on what we offer in one place and compare different options for retirement and insurance. Estimates are informational only; exact coverage is determined by eligibility policies and official plan documents. Pay Grade 16 Pay Range $44,592.00-$74,196.00 FLSA Status Exempt Job Category Administrative at-will appointment Employment Type full-time regular Job Family Environmental Safety & Police Services Job Sub Family Transportation & Parking Job Level M1 Job Open Date 08/18/2026 Posting End Date 09/08/2026 Planning Unit Vice President for Finance & Administration Work Schedule Primary shift Monday-Friday 8 AM- 5 PM. Position will require evening and weekend work at times to support operations and after-hours support. Transportation & Parking Services ( TPS ) is a 24-hour operation, 365 days a year. Position requires on-call status to respond to operational needs & service calls and work through the resolution of customer support inquiries as they arise. Months 12 month Campus Athens, Ohio Expected hours worked per week 40+ Expected duration of assignment Ongoing Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Kristen Bunce, mansfik1@ohio.edu Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio university is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio university is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Clery Act Crime Statistics Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here ! Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter References Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56807": {
      "title": "Part-time Instructor",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Part-time Instructor - Social Work (POOL POSTING) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Part-time Instructor - Social Work (POOL POSTING) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button.\r\n\r\nIf you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link.\r\nApplicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. \tThe information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of application materials will begin immediately, and the position will remain open until filled. For full consideration, please apply by February 16, 2027. Required documents to apply: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover letter List of references including contact information Unofficial graduate transcripts Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Job Title Part-time Instructor - Social Work (POOL POSTING) Applications Accepted From Public: Open to the Public Special Instructions to Applicants Review of application materials will begin immediately, and the position will remain open until filled. For full consideration, please apply by February 16, 2027. Required documents to apply: Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover letter List of references including contact information Unofficial graduate transcripts This position is eligible for the following benefits: sick leave and retirement. Posting Number 20163158F Job Description Applications to this pool will be utilized to fill part-time, non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible instructor positions on the Athens campus as student demand dictates. The number of Social Work courses offered each semester is largely dependent on student demand. Therefore, we often have the need for part-time instructors with very short notice. Such part-time positions will be filled utilizing qualified applicants from this pool. Applications will be accepted into the pool on an ongoing basis to teach practice or field courses. Instruct classes at the Graduate or Undergraduate level for Athens campus and/or online (e-campus). Minimum Qualifications Earned master’s degree in social work at the time of appointment Minimum of two years post-masters experience in social work practice Preferred Qualifications Licensed independent social worker Experience and commitment to e-learning Department Social Work Pay Rate Total Compensation Estimator (For Full-Time Benefits Eligible Employees) Discover the full value of joining Ohio University by clicking this link: https://www.ohio.edu/hr/compensation/total-compensation-estimator Our Total Compensation Estimator shows your offer package in dollars: salary plus university paid benefits including health coverage, retirement contributions, paid time off, tuition benefits, and more. See details on what we offer in one place and compare different options for retirement and insurance. Estimates are informational only; exact coverage is