    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57629": {
      "title": "Professor, Mathematics, David N. Keck Chair in Applied Analysis (Tenure Track)",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Professor, Mathematics, David N. Keck Chair in Applied Analysis (Tenure Track) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Professor, Mathematics, David N. Keck Chair in Applied Analysis (Tenure Track) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button.\r\n\r\nIf you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link.\r\nApplicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. \tThe information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete the online application and upload the following documents when prompted: Detailed cover letter Curriculum Vitae Outline of research accomplishments and plans (uploaded under the document type titled “Research Interest”) Statement of teaching philosophy and experience (uploaded under the document type titled “Teaching Philosophy Statement”) Unofficial graduate transcripts Contact information for a minimum of three professional references (uploaded under the document type titled “References”). References will only be contacted for candidates on the mid-list and with prior notice to the candidate. Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Job Title Professor, Mathematics, David N. Keck Chair in Applied Analysis (Tenure Track) Applications Accepted From Public: Open to the Public Special Instructions to Applicants Please complete the online application and upload the following documents when prompted: Detailed cover letter Curriculum Vitae Outline of research accomplishments and plans (uploaded under the document type titled “Research Interest”) Statement of teaching philosophy and experience (uploaded under the document type titled “Teaching Philosophy Statement”) Unofficial graduate transcripts Contact information for a minimum of three professional references (uploaded under the document type titled “References”). References will only be contacted for candidates on the mid-list and with prior notice to the candidate. This position is eligible for the following benefits: medical, vision, dental, basic and supplemental life, paid holidays, educational benefits for you and eligible dependents, sick leave, and retirement. Posting Number 20163230F Job Description The Department of Mathematics at Ohio University seeks applicants for the endowed David N. Keck Chair in Applied Analysis, at the rank of (full) Professor with tenure, to increase the national prominence of the college and university in this academic area. The Chair will • Guide the newly established David N. Keck Center for Applied Mathematics, • Conduct scholarly research, • Share knowledge with our university communities, • Mentor students at all levels, including directing doctoral dissertations and supervising postdoctoral researchers, • Teach undergraduate and graduate courses, and • Participate in the general activities of the department. The Chair filling this position should be well placed at the intersection of applied mathematics and analysis, especially in the development and application of differential and integral equations, dynamical systems, probability theory and stochastic processes, numerical analysis and other areas rooted in the general area of analysis. The endowment will provide core benefits to the Chair of: • A salary enhancement, • A reduction in scheduled teaching, and • Funds for travel, registrations, software, materials, visitors, publication charges, hourly undergraduate research assistants, etc. The David N. Keck Center for Applied Mathematics was established to advance research, teaching, and innovation in the field of applied mathematics by supporting faculty excellence, student development, and scholarly collaboration. In addition to the endowed Chair, the Center is expected to have sufficient funds to support • David N. Keck Postdoctoral Visiting Professors, • Research activities of member faculty, • Student research assistants, and • Other discretionary activities. The department has a broad mission, from teaching general education classes through mentoring doctoral students and conducting research. For information about our programs and faculty, see Mathematics Department | Ohio University Ohio University is a Carnegie Foundation R1 (doctoral universities – very high research activity) institution. It has a rich history, diverse campuses, international communities, and beautiful Appalachian settings. The city of Athens provides a classic and vibrant residential learning environment for over 20,000 students and is a family-friendly and culturally-rich community. The charm of tree-lined brick walkways on the University’s College Green makes you feel as if you are at a small college rather than a large university. Recently, Athens was rated the Best College Small Town by the readers of USA Today. Minimum Qualifications Required at the time of application: Ph.D. in the Mathematical Sciences or closely related fields. Achieved rank of Associate Professor with tenure at an academic institution or an equivalent government, industry, or academic position. An ongoing research program in Applied Analysis. ________________________________________________________________________________________________ Preferred Qualifications Achieved rank of (full) Professor with tenure at an academic institution or an equivalent government, industry, or academic position. Evidence of: • Outstanding research • Leadership • Teaching excellence Department Mathematics Pay Rate Salary is commensurate with experience and credentials and is accompanied by our generous university benefits such as tuition for self and dependents, a comprehensive insurance package (including but not limited to health, prescription, vision, dental, and life insurance), an excellent retirement plan including company contributions, parental leave, adoption reimbursement, and more. OHIO is also proud to offer wellness programs, on-site wellness facilities, and a generous employee assistance program. Additional Information is available at https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/ . Total Compensation Estimator (For Full-Time Benefits Eligible Employees) Discover the full value of joining Ohio University by clicking this link: https://www.ohio.edu/hr/compensation/total-compensation-estimator Our Total Compensation Estimator shows your offer package in dollars: salary plus university paid benefits including health coverage, retirement contributions, paid time off, tuition benefits, and more. See details on what we offer in one place and compare different options for retirement and insurance. Estimates are informational only; exact coverage is determined by eligibility policies and official plan documents. User Selection Field Job Open Date 09/03/2026 Posting Close Date 12/01/2026 Employment Type full-time regular Job Category Tenure Track Faculty Months 9 month Planning Unit College of Arts & Sciences Work Schedule Campus Athens, Ohio Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Joey Pierce, piercej@ohio.edu, 740-593-4565 Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio University is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio University is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Clery Act Crime Statistics Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here! Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume/Curriculum Vitae Research Interest Teaching philosophy statement Unofficial transcripts References Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
