    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57633": {
      "title": "Associate/Senior Associate Athletic Director for Business and Administrative Operations",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Associate/Senior Associate Athletic Director for Business and Administrative Operations Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Associate/Senior Associate Athletic Director for Business and Administrative Operations Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button.\r\n\r\nIf you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link.\r\nApplicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. \tThe information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply, please complete the online quick application and attach the required documents. For references, please provide names, addresses and current contact information for 3 professional references. Review of applicant materials will begin immediately and continue until a successful candidate is identified; for full consideration, please apply by 11:59 p.m., on September 11, 2026. Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Business Title Associate/Senior Associate Athletic Director for Business and Administrative Operations Applications Accepted From Public: Open to the Public Special Instructions to Applicants To apply, please complete the online quick application and attach the required documents. For references, please provide names, addresses and current contact information for 3 professional references. Review of applicant materials will begin immediately and continue until a successful candidate is identified; for full consideration, please apply by 11:59 p.m., on September 11, 2026. This position is eligible for the following benefits: medical, vision, dental, basic and supplemental life, winter break closure, paid holidays, educational benefits for you and eligible dependents, sick leave, vacation, and retirement. Posting Number 2016488T Job Description Summary Department Summary The Associate/Senior Associate Athletic Director for Business and Administrative Operations serves as a member of the department’s Athletics Executive Team and is responsible for providing strategic oversight, implementation, and management of the Department of Athletics financial functions, procedures, and policies. The position serves the role of chief financial and administrative officer ( CFAO ), maintains collaborative decision-making authority regarding the organization’s financial health, financial liaison to the University, conducts strategic financial analysis, and advises the Director of Athletics about the financial implications of operational, capital, and other strategies for the multi-million-dollar annual budget. This position provides senior level oversight of the business and administrative operations and human resources units. This position is expected to maintain a focus on continual process improvements to ensure operational efficiencies and sound financial practices. In addition, this position will provide oversight of assigned athletic sport programs, collaborating with coaches, review and monitor time management plans, develop action plans, set strategic goals, performance management and professional development, establish sport program schedules, and conduct annual performance evaluations of programs and coaches. · Responsible for directing strategic matters as they relate to budget management and control. Create financial models to perform budget forecasting and complex financial analysis necessary for departmental decisions and strategic planning, including a variety of external revenue sources, both unrestricted and restricted, such as NCAA and Mid-American Conference distributions, sponsorships, licensing, game guarantees, ticket sales and other event-related revenues, merchandise and concession commissions, gift contributions, etc. Advise the Director of Athletics with financial decisions for the multi-million-dollar annual budget. · Oversee performance of all financial responsibilities for Ohio Athletics’ administration and sport programs, including developing, maintaining, analyzing, and ensuring accountability of budgets, financial planning, and projections. Responsible for reporting forecasted results to the University Budget Office and collaborating with the Budget Office in preparation of financial forecasts for the University’s Board of Trustees. Supervise the administration of spending and expenditures for administrative and sport program units. · Collaborate with and advise the Athletics executive staff on all capital construction projects, with particular focus on identifying and directing resource allocations and project budget tracking. Ensure resources are allocated appropriately to address upkeep of equipment and facilities. · Contribute to the development of financial presentations to the Board of Trustees, Ohio University Foundation, Ohio Bobcat Club, the Ohio University Intercollegiate Athletics Committee, and other groups (as requested). · Administer internal control systems to ensure the integrity and accuracy of financial processes and records and safeguard financial assets of the department. Manage and set financial policies and procedures. Ensure compliance with institutional control by following all University, NCAA , Conference, and Federal regulations, and embracing the highest standard of integrity and ethical behavior. Works proactively to mitigate internal and external audit risks. · Maintain and coordinate accurate and timely financial reporting, including the annual Department of Education Equity in Athletics Disclosure Act ( EADA ) Report, NCAA Agreed-Upon Procedures Report, and compliance reports. · Represents the department at University-wide CFAO and other financial related meetings scheduled by senior leaders as directed by the Director of Athletics. Serves as primary contact for all financial and compliance audits. Represent the athletics department on committees throughout campus and with all external agencies, such as the NCAA and Mid-American Conference · Oversight of the Business and Administrative Operations staff with an emphasis on goal setting, delegating assignments, monitoring performance, and raising awareness and knowledge of financial management and compliance matters. · Serves as a member of the Athletics Executive Team and as a sport administrator to assigned sport programs to include personnel, budget management, competition scheduling, team athletic and academic performance, and NCAA and Mid-American Conference compliance. Position Profile Oversees, plans, manages, implements and/or evaluates the operations of a college, division, or department in the areas of human resources, compliance, financial, and additional services. Identifies and establishes financial and operational systems to monitor, control, and improve efficiency and effectiveness, not limited to, processes, procedures and policies. Level Summary Responsible for the management of a unit that performs diverse but related tasks. Handles work and budget planning, ensuring efficient allocation of resources to achieve team objectives. Contributes to divisional or departmental operational plans by aligning unit goals with broader institutional strategies. Accountable for meeting short-term objectives and driving continuous improvement. Supervisory Responsibilities Manages a large team or multiple teams. Directly oversees at least 2.0 FTE employees or one or more supervisors. Has authority to hire, transfer, suspend, promote, manage performance, discharge, assign duties, reward, and discipline employees. Fiscal Responsibilities Oversees large budgets, including departmental and program-level budgets. Problem Solving Solves strategic, organizational problems and ensures continuous improvement. Independence of Action High degree of autonomy in decision-making, accountable for large areas. Communication and Collaboration Collaborates with executive leadership and external partners to drive organizational goals. Physical Requirements This role is primarily desk-based and involves extensive use of desktop computers. Occasionally, the job may require travel to attend meetings and programs. Minimum Qualifications Requires a Master’s degree in a related field, 8 or more years of related professional experience, and 5 or more years of supervisory experience, or equivalent education and experience. Preferred Qualifications Experience in college athletics and serving as a sport administrator. Department ICA Business Administration Pay Rate The salary negotiated at the time of offer will be commensurate with education and experience. For more information on the pay structure and Pay Administration Guidelines please visit: https://www.ohio.edu/hr/compensation-pay Employees also enjoy a generous benefits package which includes medical, vision, dental, basic and supplemental life, retirement plan with a company contribution, winter break closure, paid holidays, educational benefits for you and eligible dependents, sick leave, parental leave program, vacation, and more. Additional information is available at https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits. Total Compensation Estimator (For Full-Time Benefits Eligible Employees) Discover the full value of joining Ohio University by clicking this link: https://www.ohio.edu/hr/compensation/total-compensation-estimator Our Total Compensation Estimator shows your offer package in dollars: salary plus university paid benefits including health coverage, retirement contributions, paid time off, tuition benefits, and more. See details on what we offer in one place and compare different options for retirement and insurance. Estimates are informational only; exact coverage is determined by eligibility policies and official plan documents. Pay Grade 20 Pay Range $80,593.00-$138,208.00 FLSA Status Exempt Job Category Administrative at-will appointment Employment Type full-time regular Job Family Administrative Management Job Sub Family Administrative Support Job Level M3 Job Open Date 08/21/2026 Posting End Date 09/11/2026 Planning Unit Intercollegiate Athletics Work Schedule Evenings and weekends as well as travel may be required. Months 12 month Campus Athens, Ohio Expected hours worked per week 40+ hours per week Expected duration of assignment on-going Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Trina Jones, hillt@ohio.edu Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio university is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio university is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Clery Act Crime Statistics Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here ! Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter References Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Please indicate the highest degree you have earned. No degree Associate's degree Bachelor's degree Bachelor's degree with some graduate work Master's degree Ph.D. or other terminal degree Are you a current OHIO University employee? Yes No Please indicate your level of experience within college athletics. no related experience 1 year of experience, but less than 5 5 years of experience, but less than 8 8 years of experience, but less than 10 10 years plus Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/55646": {
      "title": "Undergraduate Student Assistant, Office of Student Services",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Undergraduate Student Assistant, Office of Student Services Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Undergraduate Student Assistant, Office of Student Services Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button.\r\n\r\nIf you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link.\r\nApplicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. \tThe information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please complete the online application, submit a cover letter and resume.  Posting will remain open until it is filled. Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Business Title Undergraduate Student Assistant, Office of Student Services Special Instructions to Applicants Please complete the online application, submit a cover letter and resume.  Posting will remain open until it is filled. Posting Number 20161680STD Department Summary The Undergraduate Student Assistant serves as the first point of contact for the Office of Student Services. This position provides general office and customer service support, assisting students, faculty, staff, and visitors in a professional and welcoming manner. The ideal candidate will demonstrate strong communication skills, attention to detail, and the ability to maintain confidentiality while working in a fast-paced environment. Primary Responsibilities: Greet and assist students, visitors, and staff in person, by phone, and via email Answer general questions related to campus resources, events, and services Direct inquiries to appropriate staff members or departments Schedule appointments and maintain office calendars as needed File, scan, and organize documents; assist with mail and deliveries Help prepare materials for orientations, events, and workshops Update and maintain bulletin boards and information displays Assist with data entry, record keeping, and other clerical duties Assist with Enrollment Management, Testing Services, and Student Engagement activities as needed Support special projects and campus events coordinated through Student Services; and other duties as assigned Maintain a clean and organized front office environment Cross-trained in all operations of the Office of Student Services Required Qualifications: Must be a currently enrolled Ohio University student in good academic standing Strong interpersonal and communication skills Dependable, punctual, and professional in appearance and conduct Ability to handle confidential information appropriately Basic computer skills (Microsoft Office, Outlook, Teams, etc.) Ability to work independently and as part of a team Job Profile Duties/essential functions may include, but not be limited to, the following: Provides administrative support in an office setting, including tasks such as answering phones and emails, responding to customer inquiries, writing communications, and supporting staff with day-to-day operations. Level Summary Performs basic tasks and assists with administrative or operational duties under supervision. Roles are entry-level and aimed at providing exposure to workplace environments. Supervisory Responsibilities: Limited supervisory responsibilities. May supervise other student workers. Fiscal Responsibilities: No budgetary responsibility. Problem Solving: Addresses routine, well-defined problems under supervision. Independence of Action: Works under close supervision. Communication and Collaboration: Communicates primarily with supervisor and peers. Collaborates with team members to accomplish tasks. Minimum Qualifications Enrolled for classes at Ohio University, Hocking College, another post-secondary education institution, or a secondary school during the current semester, immediate previous semester, or immediate upcoming semester. Able to follow instructions and complete tasks within deadlines. Basic knowledge of office software and communication tools. Departments may have specific minimum requirements. Preferred Qualifications Prior customer service or office experience Working Condition/Physical Demands: This role is primarily desk-based and involves extensive use of desktop computers. Department STHRN Administrative Support Pay Rate Hourly rate based on university student employment pay scale. FLSA Status Non-Exempt Posting Open Date 11/12/2025 Posting End Date 12/12/2027 Job Category Student Hourly Planning Unit Regional Higher Education Work Schedule Flexible scheduling during normal business hours (Monday–Friday, 8:00 a.m.–5:00 p.m.) Hours arranged around class schedule Campus Southern (Ironton, Ohio) Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Robert Pleasant, pleasanr@ohio.edu, 740.533.4600 Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio University is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio university is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Employment Type Part-Time Job Level STUDENT Job Family Student Hourly Employee Job Sub Family Student Office Assistant Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here ! Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter References Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57426": {
      "title": "Student Office Assistant",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Student Office Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Student Office Assistant Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button.\r\n\r\nIf you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link.\r\nApplicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. \tThe information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note this position will work on the Chillicothe Campus. Please complete the online application and attach a resume, current semester class schedule and a cover letter indicating your interest. We are seeking candidates who have good interpersonal communication skills, the ability to work productively without close supervision, good interpersonal communication skills, basic computer literacy, attention to detail and the ability to follow procedures and confidentiality policies. Successful candidates must have and maintain a minimum cumulative GPA of 2.0 or higher. Training will be provided for applicants who are hired. Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Business Title Student Office Assistant Special Instructions to Applicants Please note this position will work on the Chillicothe Campus. Please complete the online application and attach a resume, current semester class schedule and a cover letter indicating your interest. We are seeking candidates who have good interpersonal communication skills, the ability to work productively without close supervision, good interpersonal communication skills, basic computer literacy, attention to detail and the ability to follow procedures and confidentiality policies. Successful candidates must have and maintain a minimum cumulative GPA of 2.0 or higher. Training will be provided for applicants who are hired. Posting Number 20161760STD Department Summary The OHIO Chillicothe Student Services department seeks enthusiastic and engaging students to join our teams.  Student Services Student Assistants provide support to the Student Services Department, Admissions, Shoemaker Center, and other administrative units by serving at the Bennett Hall Information Desk, Student Services Suite, and other areas of campus.  Duties may include the following: Learning and understanding campus details including units, employees, and processes in order to assist all members of the campus community. Greeting and directing campus visitors to the appropriate campus units. Answering and directing phone calls and resolving issues when possible. Processing packages accurately. Communicating with a variety of individuals and groups via speech, email, and text. Assisting with campus activities and events as needed. Monitoring the Shoemaker Center, assuring that all guests are properly checked-in. Giving campus tours and other Admissions related activities. Performing administrative tasks such as scanning, filing, organizing, and data processing. Supporting campus projects as needed. Other duties as assigned Job Profile Duties/essential functions may include, but not be limited to, the following: Provides administrative support in an office setting, including tasks such as answering phones and emails, responding to customer inquiries, writing communications, and supporting staff with day-to-day operations. Level Summary Performs basic tasks and assists with administrative or operational duties under supervision. Roles are entry-level and aimed at providing exposure to workplace environments. Supervisory Responsibilities: Limited supervisory responsibilities. May supervise other student workers. Fiscal Responsibilities: No budgetary responsibility. Problem Solving: Addresses routine, well-defined problems under supervision. Independence of Action: Works under close supervision. Communication and Collaboration: Communicates primarily with supervisor and peers. Collaborates with team members to accomplish tasks. Minimum Qualifications Enrolled for classes at Ohio University, Hocking College, another post-secondary education institution, or a secondary school during the current semester, immediate previous semester, or immediate upcoming semester. Able to follow instructions and complete tasks within deadlines. Basic knowledge of office software and communication tools. Departments may have specific minimum requirements. Preferred Qualifications Working Condition/Physical Demands: This role is primarily desk-based and involves extensive use of desktop computers. Occasionally, the job may require travel to attend meetings and programs. Department CHILI Student Services-Advising Pay Rate $11.00 PER HR FLSA Status Non-Exempt Posting Open Date 08/10/2026 Posting End Date 11/30/2026 Job Category Student Hourly Planning Unit Regional Higher Education Work Schedule Work hours are flexible but must be willing to work morning and evening hours as needed. Campus Chillicothe, Ohio Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Ashlee Tatman, tatman@ohio.edu, 740-774-7229 Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio University is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio university is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Employment Type Part-Time Job Level STUDENT Job Family Student Hourly Employee Job Sub Family Student Office Assistant Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here ! Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter STUDENT Class Schedule Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
