    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57295": {
      "title": "Student IT Support Specialist (ZANESVILLE CAMPUS)",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Student IT Support Specialist (ZANESVILLE CAMPUS) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Student IT Support Specialist (ZANESVILLE CAMPUS) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button.\r\n\r\nIf you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link.\r\nApplicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. \tThe information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note this position will work on the Zanesville Campus of Ohio University. Please complete the online application and attach a resume, current semester class schedule and a cover letter indicating your interest. We are seeking candidates who have good interpersonal communication skills, the ability to work productively without close supervision and the ability to follow confidentiality policies. Successful candidates must have and maintain a minimum cumulative GPA of 2.0 or higher. Training will be provided for applicants who are hired. Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Business Title Student IT Support Specialist (ZANESVILLE CAMPUS) Special Instructions to Applicants Please note this position will work on the Zanesville Campus of Ohio University. Please complete the online application and attach a resume, current semester class schedule and a cover letter indicating your interest. We are seeking candidates who have good interpersonal communication skills, the ability to work productively without close supervision and the ability to follow confidentiality policies. Successful candidates must have and maintain a minimum cumulative GPA of 2.0 or higher. Training will be provided for applicants who are hired. Posting Number 20161752STD Department Summary The Ohio University Zanesville Campus invites applications for the position of Student IT Support Specialist. This position will work on the Zanesville campus which is located in Zanesville, Ohio. Specific departmental duties may include: Help Desk Support · Answering the help desk phone, entering work orders, and resolving issues when possible · Check out and deliver equipment · Assisting with inventory, testing, and cleaning of computer equipment. · Supporting campus projects as needed OULN Classroom Operator Support · Responsible to be sure equipment is powered, connected and functioning for class · Distribute and collect papers, assignments, etc. before class and return to the proper department/location immediately after class · Log any classroom technical issues and relay information to appropriate support team using the Teams application Campus Event Support · Setup computer, audio and AV equipment for scheduled campus events · Operate equipment during event · Troubleshoot any issues and resolve as necessary · Return equipment to appropriate storage location(s) when event ends Job Profile Duties/essential functions may include, but not be limited to, the following: Provides technical assistance to students, staff, and faculty by troubleshooting software or hardware issues, maintaining IT systems, and offering solutions to ensure smooth technological operations across the University. Provides an entry point into the field of Information Technology for Ohio University students. Level Summary Performs basic tasks and assists with administrative or operational duties under supervision. Roles are entry-level and aimed at providing exposure to workplace environments. Supervisory Responsibilities: Limited supervisory responsibilities. May supervise other student workers. Fiscal Responsibilities: No budgetary responsibility. Problem Solving: Addresses routine, well-defined problems under supervision. Independence of Action: Works under close supervision. Communication and Collaboration: Communicates primarily with supervisor and peers. Collaborates with team members to accomplish tasks. Minimum Qualifications Enrolled for classes at Ohio University, Hocking College, another post-secondary education institution, or a secondary school during the current semester, immediate previous semester, or immediate upcoming semester. Able to follow instructions and complete tasks within deadlines. Basic knowledge of office software and communication tools. Departments may have specific minimum requirements. Preferred Qualifications Working Condition/Physical Demands: This role is primarily desk-based and involves extensive use of desktop computers. Occasionally, the job may require travel to attend meetings and programs. Department Regional Higher Education Pay Rate $11.00 per hour FLSA Status Non-Exempt Posting Open Date 07/28/2026 Posting End Date 11/30/2026 Job Category Student Hourly Planning Unit Regional Higher Education Work Schedule Work hours are flexible but must be willing to work morning and evening hours as needed. Campus Zanesville, Ohio Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Steve Fraunfelter, steve.fraunfelter@ohio.edu Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio University is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio university is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Employment Type Part-Time Job Level STUDENT Job Family Student Hourly Employee Job Sub Family Student IT Support Specialist Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here ! Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter STUDENT Class Schedule Optional Documents References Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56307": {
      "title": "Teacher Education Instructor, Reading Education, part-time [Pool Posting]",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Teacher Education Instructor, Reading Education, part-time [Pool Posting] Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Teacher Education Instructor, Reading Education, part-time [Pool Posting] Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button.\r\n\r\nIf you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link.\r\nApplicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. \tThe information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The Department of Teacher Education is accepting applications for potential Instructor openings for courses in Reading Education for the academic year 2026-2027. The need for these positions is undetermined at this time and is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will select candidates from this pool posting. Application to this pool will be utilized to fill part-time, non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible instructor positions on the Athens campus as student demand dictates for fall and spring semesters. To apply, please complete the online application and upload required documents including resume/CV, detailed letter of Interest, list of at least 3 professional references with full current contact information including email address, and a document outlining your availability to teach for fall semester (August 24, 2026- December 13, 3026) and spring semester (January 11, 2027 – April 30, 2027. Please apply by 3/2/2027. Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Job Title Teacher Education Instructor, Reading Education, part-time [Pool Posting] Applications Accepted From Public: Open to the Public Special Instructions to Applicants The Department of Teacher Education is accepting applications for potential Instructor openings for courses in Reading Education for the academic year 2026-2027. The need for these positions is undetermined at this time and is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will select candidates from this pool posting. Application to this pool will be utilized to fill part-time, non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible instructor positions on the Athens campus as student demand dictates for fall and spring semesters. To apply, please complete the online application and upload required documents including resume/CV, detailed letter of Interest, list of at least 3 professional references with full current contact information including email address, and a document outlining your availability to teach for fall semester (August 24, 2026- December 13, 3026) and spring semester (January 11, 2027 – April 30, 2027. Please apply by 3/2/2027. This position is eligible for the following benefits: sick leave and retirement. Posting Number 20163096F Job Description The Gladys W. and David H. Patton College of Education prepares graduates who are CALLED to LEAD : Change Agents who are Lifelong Learners committed to Embracing Diversity and LEADership. Our leader-educators, practitioners, and human service professionals share our commitment to serving society responsibly as change agents in meeting diverse human and social needs. The number of Teacher Education courses offered each semester is dependent on student demand. The need may include both graduate and undergraduate courses in Reading Education. The successful applicant will bring strong qualifications both academically and professionally. Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses on campus and/or online. Contribute to the instructional mission of the Teacher Education Department and Patton College of Education. Using Canvas for academic engagement Minimum Qualifications Master’s degree in the field or comparable Current or prior teaching license Experience teaching students for that field Experience using technology for teaching Training/experience in the Science of Reading Preferred Qualifications Relevant and recent Pre K-12 classroom based experience Demonstrated knowledge of theory and research-supported best practices for teaching and learning Licensure in content area Experience facilitating professional development Evidence of professional training or attendance and/or presentations at conferences Ability to deliver online instruction Department Teacher Education Pay Rate Total Compensation Estimator (For Full-Time Benefits Eligible Employees) Discover the full value of joining Ohio University by clicking this link: https://www.ohio.edu/hr/compensation/total-compensation-estimator Our Total Compensation Estimator shows your offer package in dollars: salary plus university paid benefits including health coverage, retirement contributions, paid time off, tuition benefits, and more. See details on what we offer in one place and compare different options for retirement and insurance. Estimates are informational only; exact coverage is determined by eligibility policies and official plan documents. User Selection Field Job Open Date 03/16/2026 Posting Close Date Please apply by 03/02/2027 Employment Type Temporary (for group 3 ONLY) Job Category Instructor Months 4 month Planning Unit Patton College of Education Work Schedule Campus Athens, Ohio Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Jennifer Martin, martinj8@ohio.edu Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio University is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio University is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Clery Act Crime Statistics Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here! Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter References Other (See Special Instructions to Applicants for Details) Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
