ument that details your teaching capabilities and attach it as an “other” document. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue as needs arise throughout the year. Please apply by the posting closing date. Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Job Title Arts Administration On-Campus Instructors (POOL POSTING) Applications Accepted From Public: Open to the Public Special Instructions to Applicants This is a pool posting for potential Instructor needs that may arise for Academic Year 2026-27. The need for these positions is undetermined at this time and is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will select candidates from this posting. Please complete the online application, attach the following documents: Current resume/CV List of three professional references including current contact information. Interested candidates should also include a document that details your teaching capabilities and attach it as an “other” document. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue as needs arise throughout the year. Please apply by the posting closing date. This position is eligible for the following benefits: sick leave and retirement. Posting Number 20163154F Job Description This is a pool posting for potential Instructor needs that may arise for Academic Year 2026-27 in Arts Administration. This posting is for teaching in-person synchronous courses at the Athens campus. Course topics will vary based on need, but may include “Intro to Arts Administration”, “Funding and Development for Arts Organizations”, and “Concepts, Communications, Considerations in Arts Management” Minimum Qualifications A Master’s Degree in Arts Administration (or related field) by the start date of appointment, or an equivalent amount of professional practice or experience in accordance with Ohio University policy