    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57565": {
      "title": "Events Manager",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Events Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Events Manager Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button.\r\n\r\nIf you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link.\r\nApplicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. \tThe information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested individuals should complete an online application and be prepared to upload the following documents at the time of application: 1. Current CV or Resume 2. Cover letter summarizing interest and qualifications for the role 3. List of 3 professional references including current telephone and email addresses for all references. For full consideration, please submit your materials by position closing date Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Business Title Events Manager Applications Accepted From University Wide, Public: Open to the Public Special Instructions to Applicants Interested individuals should complete an online application and be prepared to upload the following documents at the time of application: 1. Current CV or Resume 2. Cover letter summarizing interest and qualifications for the role 3. List of 3 professional references including current telephone and email addresses for all references. For full consideration, please submit your materials by position closing date This position is eligible for the following benefits: medical, vision, dental, basic and supplemental life, winter break closure, paid holidays, educational benefits for you and eligible dependents, sick leave, vacation, and retirement. Posting Number 2016480T Job Description Summary Department Summary The Events Manager is responsible for the oversight, coordination, and continuous improvement of campus event parking operations, event logistics, and parking support activities. This position is responsible for the planning & coordination support activities of parking accommodations for athletic events, campus lot and meter reservations, conferences, and large university functions such as commencement, move in/move out and performing arts events and provides back-up support for parking support needs. Position Responsibilities: Provides leadership and oversight for campus events and parking support activities and is responsible for the strategic planning, management, execution, and continuous improvement activities associated with event parking operations. Works all assigned events, providing onsite leadership during these events to ensure operational success, provide customer support, and address inquiries or concerns from guests. Acts as the frontline events ambassador for TPS , modeling professional conduct and service excellence. Accountable for achieving established performance measures related to event execution, customer satisfaction, revenue generation, meeting designated budget, staffing effectiveness, operational efficiency, and service quality. Plans, coordinates and schedules reservation requests for lot/space closures, meter reservations, guest accommodations, permit requests, and parking support accommodations submitted by internal and external customers. Develops and implements equipment and field logistics plans to support event operations. Working closely with the Parking Field Operations Manager to ensure successful field execution of event closures, signage, and equipment Serves as the primary point of contact with Athletics to understand event needs, plan parking operations and ensure alignment with TPS resources and capabilities for OHIO athletic events. Develops and maintains partnerships with external organizations and agencies hosting events on campus including organizations such as the Ohio High School Athletic Association ( OHSAA ) to plan parking, traffic management, and event logistic requirements to support event needs. Assists campus stakeholders with developing and enacting parking plans to support major university events such as commencement, move in/move out, performing arts events, campus recreation events, admissions/ BSO , camps/conferences and other high impact campus activities. Manage and maintains event parking technology including handheld devices, POS systems, PCI requirements, and mobile applications used for event access and field payment collection. Prepares and submits financial deposits for event parking operations in accordance with fiscal procedures. Prepares and distributes weekly lot closure emails and event specific communications for the campus community, event planners, and partners. Leads regularly established event coordination meetings with internal campus units and stakeholders to review event logistics and maintain partnerships. Represents Transportation & Parking Services in university, community, and event planning meetings with internal and external stakeholders to ensure seamless event execution and operational collaboration. Develop and distribute post-event reports, summarizing operations, revenue, and staffing and monitors and reports on KPI’s to drive revenue growth, operational efficiency, and cost containment strategies. Develops and distributes event operational service guides and planning documents, policies, and best practice documentation. Develop and maintain standard operating procedures and training materials to ensure consistency and continuity of operations. Completes benchmarking studies, and market research to identify trends, maintain competitiveness, and implement improvement strategies. Provides backup support for campus parking operations and customer service functions. Responsible for hiring, scheduling, supervision, performance management and development for operations team including 6-8 student event managers and 50-100 student event staff. Directs the daily operations of assigned staff and ensures resources are available to achieve work plans and resolve complex business needs. Ensures staff adherence to standard operating procedures and service guidelines and compliance with university, state and federal service requirements. Proactively works to diffuse potential conflict before it begins. Oversees integration of event parking technologies with existing parking management infrastructure. Remain current with emerging technologies and industry best practices to optimize service. Serves as the primary point of contact for after-hours support/resolution for assigned programs. Displays leadership that results in teamwork, customer focus, innovation and continuous process improvement within their organization. Serves as a liaison for Transportation & Parking Services operations, representing the unit in a professional and customer-centric manner. Assists with documentation of standard operating procedures, departmental guidelines, professional development and training, and safety/emergency procedures for operations activities & personnel in compliance with university, state/federal regulations. Maintains operational inventories. Supports special projects and initiatives for unit and RFP’s for technology and services as assigned. Provides support and assist with departmental functions as needed. Performs other misc. duties as assigned. Works to resolve complex service issues & ensure operational efficiency and high levels of customer service with minimal impact to business operations and service functions. Position Profile Monitors campus transportation and parking activities and compliance with established policies. Responsible for overseeing permit parking, parking enforcement, event transportation, business transportation, campus transit service, safety and training, and facility and operations maintenance. Level Summary Supervises a team and ensures effective work activities within work unit. Has input on personnel actions for direct reports. Primarily focused on supervision, but may still engage in operational tasks similar to the direct reports’ roles. Accountable for the productivity and effectiveness of the team or department, ensuring goals are met. Supervisory Responsibilities Manages a small team. Directly oversees at least 2.0 FTE employees. Has authority to manage performance and assign duties. May have authority to hire, transfer, suspend, promote, discharge, reward, and discipline employees. Fiscal Responsibilities Responsible for managing a small budget or part of a larger budget. Problem Solving Solves interpersonal team issues and develops solutions for team-related problems. Seeks guidance from higher-level management on complex problems. Independence of Action Has discretion in decision-making but reports to higher-level management. Communication and Collaboration Collaborates with higher-level manager(s) and other teams, ensures team alignment with organizational goals. Physical Requirements Requires a range of physical activities. Positions may require driving, standing, walking through parking facilities, and/or ascending stairs or ramps. Minimum Qualifications Requires a Bachelor’s degree in a related field, 3 or more years of related professional experience, and 1 or more years of supervisory experience, or equivalent education and experience. Certain positions may require Commercial Driver’s License ( CDL ). Must possess a valid Driver’s license. Preferred Qualifications Strong oral and written communications and must have proficient knowledge in Microsoft Office and technology. Experience with parking and event management technologies. Ability to work under pressure managing multiple service priorities, strong interpersonal, organizational and teamwork skills. Department Transportation & Parking Pay Rate The target salary range is $44,592 to $59,085 commensurate with the selected candidate’s education and experience while considering internal equity. Ohio University is proud to offer a robust healthcare plan that includes maternity care, counseling and mental healthcare, prescription coverage, vision, dental, orthodontia care, and more. Our robust benefits package also includes paid holidays, sick time, personal time, a tuition waiver up to 100% for self and dependents, an excellent retirement plan with up to a 14% employer contribution, a 12-week parental leave program, adoption reimbursement, flextime and flexplace policies, an employee assistance program, access to professional development programs, and additional employee resources. Additional information is available at https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits . Total Compensation Estimator (For Full-Time Benefits Eligible Employees) Discover the full value of joining Ohio University by clicking this link: https://www.ohio.edu/hr/compensation/total-compensation-estimator Our Total Compensation Estimator shows your offer package in dollars: salary plus university paid benefits including health coverage, retirement contributions, paid time off, tuition benefits, and more. See details on what we offer in one place and compare different options for retirement and insurance. Estimates are informational only; exact coverage is determined by eligibility policies and official plan documents. Pay Grade 16 Pay Range $44,592.00-$74,196.00 FLSA Status Exempt Job Category Administrative at-will appointment Employment Type full-time regular Job Family Environmental Safety & Police Services Job Sub Family Transportation & Parking Job Level M1 Job Open Date 08/18/2026 Posting End Date 09/23/2026 Planning Unit Vice President for Finance & Administration Work Schedule Primary shift Monday-Friday 8 AM- 5 PM. Position requires non-traditional hours, including evenings, nights, and weekends, based on event schedule demands. Must have ability to work nights, weekends, and extended hours during peak event seasons. Transportation & Parking Services ( TPS ) is a 24-hour operation, 365 days a year. Position requires on-call status to respond to operational needs & service calls and work through the resolution of customer support inquiries as they arise. Months 12 month Campus Athens, Ohio Expected hours worked per week 40+ Expected duration of assignment Ongoing Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Tia Hysell, prattt@ohio.edu Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio university is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio university is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Clery Act Crime Statistics Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here ! Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter References Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
