    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/56850": {
      "title": "Instructor, English (Part-time, Non-tenure track) POOL POSTING",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Instructor, English (Part-time, Non-tenure track) POOL POSTING Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Instructor, English (Part-time, Non-tenure track) POOL POSTING Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button.\r\n\r\nIf you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link.\r\nApplicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. \tThe information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. We are accepting resumes/CVs for potential openings in the Department of English for the Fall 2026 semester and the 2026-2027 academic year. Applications to this pool will be considered to fill part-time, non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible instructor positions at the Athens campus. The need for these positions is undetermined at this time and is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will review and select candidates from this posting. Applications will be accepted into the pool on an ongoing basis through the close date listed in this posting. Please complete the online application and upload: Letter of interest A current Curriculum Vitae Unofficial copies of graduate transcripts Evidence of teaching effectiveness, if available A list of three professional references, including their current contact information Evidence of teaching effectiveness should be combined as one document and uploaded under the document type of “Other”. Good evidence of teaching effectiveness would include a syllabus and corresponding set of course evaluations, if available. Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Job Title Instructor, English (Part-time, Non-tenure track) POOL POSTING Applications Accepted From Public: Open to the Public Special Instructions to Applicants We are accepting resumes/CVs for potential openings in the Department of English for the Fall 2026 semester and the 2026-2027 academic year. Applications to this pool will be considered to fill part-time, non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible instructor positions at the Athens campus. The need for these positions is undetermined at this time and is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will review and select candidates from this posting. Applications will be accepted into the pool on an ongoing basis through the close date listed in this posting. Please complete the online application and upload: Letter of interest A current Curriculum Vitae Unofficial copies of graduate transcripts Evidence of teaching effectiveness, if available A list of three professional references, including their current contact information Evidence of teaching effectiveness should be combined as one document and uploaded under the document type of “Other”. Good evidence of teaching effectiveness would include a syllabus and corresponding set of course evaluations, if available. This position is eligible for the following benefits: sick leave and retirement. Posting Number 20163168F Job Description The English department is seeking applicants for a part-time, non-tenure track, non-benefits eligible instructor position at the Athens campus for the Fall 2026 semester and the 2026-2027 academic year. The need for these positions is undetermined at this time and is dependent on operational need including enrollment and staffing. If a need arises, the department will review and select candidates from this posting. Applications will be accepted into the pool on an ongoing basis through the close date listed in this posting. The instructor will teach first-year and/or advanced composition or another writing or literature course as assigned. Please see https://www.ohio.edu/cas/english for details about the English program. English Department: The Department of English has 29 full-time faculty across the main campus and seven regional campuses and centers in Southern and Central Ohio. Situated within the College of Arts & Sciences, the Department is committed to excellence in teaching, research, and service to the students it serves in the undergraduate major, M.A. and Ph.D. degree programs, and across the university in writing and humanities general education courses. To learn more about the successes of our English Department and student programs, visit; https://www.ohio.edu/cas/english . College of Arts & Sciences: This college is central to Ohio University’s transformative learning experience. The foundational instruction for the entire university, delivered through the general education and liberal arts curriculum, is provided by the College of Arts and Sciences. The college provides the primary instruction for approximately one-third of the undergraduate majors on campus, as well as half of the undergraduate credit hours on the Athens campus. In addition, the college offers a number of master’s programs, and eight departments offer doctoral degrees. A&S faculty are at the heart of Ohio University’s research activity. Ohio University. Established in 1804, Ohio University is the oldest public university in the state of Ohio. Our total enrollment is over 28,000 students across the state and online. About 20,000 of those students are undergraduates studying at our residential campus in Athens—our quintessential college town that’s nestled deep in the Appalachian foothills of beautiful Southeast Ohio. Our picturesque campus is located in the foothills of the Appalachian Mountains amidst scenic state and national parks, and is just 75 minutes southeast of Columbus, Ohio. Minimum Qualifications MA in English, or minimally a master’s degree and a cohesive set of 18 semester credit hours of discipline relevant graduate course work by start date of the appointment. Preferred Qualifications Experience with teaching of writing. Previous experience teaching English courses at Ohio University. Department English Pay Rate Pay is set according to college approved rates. Please visit A&S Summer and Overload Course Policy | Ohio University for more information. Pay is accompanied by an excellent retirement plan and paid sick time. Total Compensation Estimator (For Full-Time Benefits Eligible Employees) Discover the full value of joining Ohio University by clicking this link: https://www.ohio.edu/hr/compensation/total-compensation-estimator Our Total Compensation Estimator shows your offer package in dollars: salary plus university paid benefits including health coverage, retirement contributions, paid time off, tuition benefits, and more. See details on what we offer in one place and compare different options for retirement and insurance. Estimates are informational only; exact coverage is determined by eligibility policies and official plan documents. User Selection Field Job Open Date 06/03/2026 Posting Close Date 05/30/2027 Employment Type Temporary (for group 3 ONLY) Job Category Instructor Months variable month Planning Unit College of Arts & Sciences Work Schedule Campus Athens, Ohio Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Nancy Vandeman, vandemn1@ohio.edu Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio University is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio University is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Clery Act Crime Statistics Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here! Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter References Unofficial transcripts Optional Documents Other (See Special Instructions to Applicants for Details) Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57630": {
      "title": "Accounting Support Senior Specialist",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Accounting Support Senior Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Accounting Support Senior Specialist Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button.\r\n\r\nIf you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link.\r\nApplicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. \tThe information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position is being posted internally and to the public simultaneously in order to expedite the posting process. However, internal Ohio University AFSCME 3200 applicants will be considered first. Please complete the online application and attach required documents. Required documents include: A detailed cover letter Resume A list of at least three (3) professional references with current contact details, including email addresses. For additional details, please review the College of Arts & Sciences Finance Unit Web Page: A&S Finance Unit | Ohio University We seek candidates with a commitment to working effectively with students, faculty and staff from diverse background. Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Job Title Accounting Support Senior Specialist Applications Accepted From Public: Open to the public , University Wide, AFSCME 3200 University Wide Special Instructions to Applicants This position is being posted internally and to the public simultaneously in order to expedite the posting process. However, internal Ohio University AFSCME 3200 applicants will be considered first. Please complete the online application and attach required documents. Required documents include: A detailed cover letter Resume A list of at least three (3) professional references with current contact details, including email addresses. For additional details, please review the College of Arts & Sciences Finance Unit Web Page: A&S Finance Unit | Ohio University We seek candidates with a commitment to working effectively with students, faculty and staff from diverse background. This position is eligible for the following benefits: medical, vision, dental, basic and supplemental life, winter break closure, paid holidays, educational benefits for you and eligible dependents, sick leave, vacation, and retirement. Posting Number 20167041S Job Description Supports the organization’s accounting functions. Maintains up-to-date and accurate records of daily transactions, accounts receivable, accounts payable, inventories, payroll, and various other records. •Serves as the initial contact for customers. Mentors, coaches, and trains lower level employees on customer service and department policies. •Often directs work, trains, and/or supervises other staff or student employees. •Performs financial analyses and makes recommendations based on data. •Reviews the work of other employees for accuracy and compliance with accepted standards and University policies. •Completes and submits institutional surveys for publishers and agencies. •Issues purchase orders in accordance with functional policy. Communicates with internal and external customers to manage purchasing. •Analyzes and monitors department and program budgets. Approves and tracks expenditures. Minimum Qualifications Knowledge of finance and business technical and practical concepts, processes, and methods typically obtained by a high school degree or GED or equivalent and a minimum of 5 years of related experience. An equivalent combination of education, training, and experience is acceptable. Specific knowledge, certifications, and licensure will apply at the position level. Preferred Qualifications Experience in an academic support unit. Experience providing grant management support, including monitoring expenditures, maintaining grant records, and assisting with compliance and reporting requirements. Experience using university financial systems and enterprise administrative platforms is preferred, along with proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, particularly Excel, Word, and Outlook. Working Conditions/Physical Demands This position requires extensive and sustained use of a computer and related technology to perform essential job duties, including accessing and managing electronic records, communicating electronically, and using specialized software and online systems. Department Arts and Sciences, Dean's Office Pay Rate The starting salary range is $16.84 per hour up to $21.48 per hour, dependent on education and prior experience and is accompanied by our generous university benefits such as tuition for self and dependents, a comprehensive insurance package (including but not limited to health, prescription, vision, dental, and life insurance), an excellent retirement plan including company contributions, parental leave, adoption reimbursement, and more. OHIO is also proud to offer wellness programs, on-site wellness facilities, and a generous employee assistance program. Additional Information is available at: https://www.ohio.edu/hr/benefits/ . Total Compensation Estimator (For Full-Time Benefits Eligible Employees) Discover the full value of joining Ohio University by clicking this link: https://www.ohio.edu/hr/compensation/total-compensation-estimator Our Total Compensation Estimator shows your offer package in dollars: salary plus university paid benefits including health coverage, retirement contributions, paid time off, tuition benefits, and more. See details on what we offer in one place and compare different options for retirement and insurance. Estimates are informational only; exact coverage is determined by eligibility policies and official plan documents. Job Open Date 08/28/2026 Posting Close Date 09/13/2026 Job Category Classified AFSCME 3200 Bargaining Unit appointment Months Planning Unit College of Arts & Sciences Work Schedule Standard office hours are Monday–Friday, 8:00 a.m.–5:00 p.m. Upon successful completion of the probationary period, there may be an opportunity to work remotely one day per week, subject to departmental needs and approval. Campus Athens, Ohio Expected hours worked per week 40 Expected duration of assignment Ongoing Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Joey Pierce, Employment Coordinator, piercej@ohio.edu Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio University is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio university is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Job Information Employment Type full-time regular Job Family/Subfamily Finance and Business-Accounting Support Career Track & Level TAS4 Pay Grade AF3200 |14| Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here! Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter References Optional Documents Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Please indicate how you learned about this posting. www. ohiouniversityjobs.com www.higheredjobs.com www.ohiomeansjobs.com The Athens Messenger The Chronicle of Higher Education Ohio University employee OHIO Jobs Line (phone) Employment Agency Posted Announcement Professional association Social Media (LinkedIn, Twitter, etc) OTHER * Please indicate your highest level of education. no HS diploma or GED HS diploma or GED Associate's degree Bachelor's degree Bachelor's degree plus some work towards graduate degree Master's degree Ph.D. or equivalent Will have earned Ph.D. by time of appointment * Please select an option that best represents your current status: I am a current Ohio University employee and NOT currently serving a probationary period. I am a current Ohio University employee, and I am serving in either an initial or a promotional probationary period. I am a current Ohio University Student employee. I am not an employee of Ohio University. * Are you a current Ohio University AFSCME 3200 employee who is not serving in an initial probationary period? yes no * Please indicate your level of experience with administrative support / office management. no related experience less than 1 year at least 1 year, but less than 3 years at least 3 years, but less than 5 years at least 5 years, but less than 7 years 7 or more years * Do you have experience working in an academic setting? If so, please describe fully. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe your experience using university financial systems and Microsoft Office applications, particularly Word, Excel, OneDrive, and Teams. Please indicate your level of proficiency with each. (Open Ended Question) Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
