    "https://www.ohiouniversityjobs.com/postings/57575": {
      "title": "Student Admissions Assistant",
      "description": "Ohio University - Job Site | Student Admissions Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Take a virtual tour of OHIO Explore Athens County Ohio University Home Office of Civil Rights Compliance Ohio University Human Resources Total Compensation Estimator Student Employment Dual Career Network Equal Employment and Educational Opportunity Policy Notice of Non-Discrimination Annual Security and Fire Safety Report OH/Western PA/WV Higher Education Recruitment Consortium HERC Student Admissions Assistant Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button.\r\n\r\nIf you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link.\r\nApplicant Portal Voluntary Demographics. \tThe information requested below is used to assist us in our compliance with Federal/State equal employment opportunity record keeping and reporting. Your response is voluntary and will not be used in any way to determine your eligibility for employment. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Applications will be accepted until midnight (Eastern Time Zone) on the ‘Posting End Date’ shown below. Position Information Business Title Student Admissions Assistant Special Instructions to Applicants Posting Number 20161769STD Department Summary Student Admissions Assistants “Ambassadors” serve as the student face of Ohio University Southern by welcoming prospective students and families, supporting recruitment initiatives, and promoting the university throughout the Tri-State region. Through conversations and peer-to-peer engagement, ambassadors help prospective students explore educational opportunities, navigate the enrollment process, and envision themselves as future Bobcats. Student Ambassadors work collaboratively with Admissions, the Office of Student Services, faculty, and campus partners to support recruitment events, campus visits, community outreach, and student engagement activities while fostering a welcoming and inclusive campus environment. Job Profile Duties/essential functions may include, but not be limited to, the following: Supports the admissions office by processing applications, assisting prospective students and other guests with inquiries, scheduling and conducting campus tours, and providing general administrative support in the admissions process. Represents and communicates the unique student experience at Ohio University. May participate in daily visits, large special visit programs, special group visits, individual VIP tours, and question-and-answer panels. May staff office front desks to welcome and serve campus guests. May conduct out-bound calls to prospective and admitted students family members. May assist with managing inboud emails. Level Summary Performs basic tasks and assists with administrative or operational duties under supervision. The role is entry-level and aimed at providing exposure to workplace environments. Supervisory Responsibilities: Limited supervisory responsibilities. May supervise other student workers. Fiscal Responsibilities: No budgetary responsibility. Problem Solving: Addresses routine, well-defined problems under supervision. Independence of Action: Works under close supervision. Communication and Collaboration: Communicates primarily with supervisor and peers. Collaborates with team members to accomplish tasks. Communicates externally with prospective students, family members, and other influencers in the college decision making process. Minimum Qualifications Enrolled for classes at Ohio University during the current semester or immediate previous semester. Able to follow instructions and complete tasks within deadlines. Basic knowledge of office software and communication tools. Departments may have specific minimum requirements. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Working Condition/Physical Demands: This role requires ability to provide walking tours of campus and escorts guests to various locations across campus, stand for extended periods of time to direct visitors and guests, sit at a desk for extended periods with extensive use of a computer. Occasionally, the job may require travel off-campus to attend meetings and programs. Work Schedule/Location: Responsibilities generally occur between the hours of 8 am and 8 pm Monday through Saturday. However, there may be some work required earlier than 8 am or later than 8 pm or on Sundays. Department Admissions Pay Rate Hourly rate based on university student employment pay scale. FLSA Status Non-Exempt Posting Open Date 08/28/2026 Posting End Date 12/01/2026 Job Category Student Hourly Planning Unit Vice President Enrollment Management Work Schedule 10–20 hours per week, depending on recruitment and campus programming needs. Availability to support evening and weekend recruitment and student engagement activities, as needed. Campus Southern (Ironton, Ohio) Applicants may contact this person if they have questions about this position. Jesse \"Tyler\" Grubbs Non-Discrimination Statement Ohio University is proud of its rich history and as part of our ongoing efforts to provide and support a transformative learning experience, we affirm our commitment to fostering a welcoming and respectful workforce and community. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration free from discrimination on the basis of age, ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity or expression, genetic information, military service or veteran status, national origin, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, status as a parent or foster parent, or any other bases under the law. Ohio university is an equal access/equal opportunity employer. Employment Type Part-Time Job Level STUDENT Job Family Student Hourly Employee Job Sub Family Student Admissions Assistant Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Clery Act Statistics To view the Clery Act Annual Safety and Fire Report Click Here ! Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter References Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Ohio University Human Resources | Grosvenor West 103 | 1 Ohio University | Athens, OH 45701| T: 740.593.1636 | F: 740.593.0386 Ohio University | Athens OH 45701 | 740.593.1000 ADA Compliance | © 2011 Ohio University. All rights reserved. uhr@ohio.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
